# Environment scheme (ACCESS-SECURITY-OPS §C.2). Key names and comments only: never put a value in
# this file. Database names are committed constants in shared/stdb-targets.ts, not env vars:
#   test = hsr-spacetimedb-test1, prod = hsr-spacetimedb-prod (host wss://maincloud.spacetimedb.com).
#
# Where things run (A174): Vercel is production only (the prod database). Everything that touches
# the test database runs on this machine: `npm run dev`, `npm run preview`, the scripts, the tests.

# ─── Target selector (not a secret) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Node side (scripts, test harness): `--target test|prod` on every scripts/stdb/*.ts call, or
# STDB_TARGET in the shell. The flag wins; neither → the script refuses to guess.
# The login function reads the same key: on Vercel STDB_TARGET=prod (a project setting); on this
# machine the local runner sets test itself (dev and preview are test only).
# STDB_TARGET=

# ─── Browser (Vite) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_STDB_TARGET=test|prod. web/.env.development sets test for `npm run dev`; `npm run preview`
# builds with test; the Vercel project sets prod. A build without it fails.
# Never give a secret a VITE_ name: Vite puts every VITE_ value into the public bundle
# (check:patterns gate 10 refuses a VITE_ variant of the secret keys under web/).
# VITE_STDB_TARGET=

# ─── .env.test.local and .env.prod.local (gitignored by .env*.local) ─────────
# One file per database; the key names are the same in both.
#
# Written by `npm run stdb:bootstrap:<target>` (do not edit these lines by hand; bootstrap keeps
# every other line of the file):
# STDB_SERVER_TOKEN=      delegate token for the server_* reducers (scripts only, Admin level;
#                         never given to the login function or to Vercel)
# STDB_SERVER_IDENTITY=   that delegate's identity (lets the next bootstrap revoke it)
# STDB_LINK_TOKEN=        the login function's Linker token: it can only present a sign-in code,
#                         but holding it is enough to sign in as any Discord-linked account, so it
#                         is a high-value secret (docs/auth/architecture.md "The link token")
# STDB_LINK_IDENTITY=     that linker's identity (kept across bootstrap runs; --rotate-linker mints a new one)
#
# Pasted by you into .env.test.local, for login tests on localhost (npm run dev / npm run preview).
# Paste each value bare, without quotes: the local reader keeps quote characters as part of the
# value. Spaces around a value are trimmed; a value of only spaces counts as missing.
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=      the Discord application's client id (one application serves test and
#                         prod, A175: this is also the live value)
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=  that application's client secret (the live one too)
# AUTH_SECRET=            at least 32 random characters (not one character repeated); seals the
#                         OAuth state cookie. Generate it randomly (the length check cannot spot
#                         every weak value), and use a different value per environment
# (No AUTH_ORIGIN locally: the local runner uses its own address, localhost or 127.0.0.1.)
#
# Optional, test only (tools/capture-ws-frames.ts): CAPTURE_WS_FIXTURE_TOKEN= (a guest token)

# ─── Login function on Vercel (production) ───────────────────────────────────
# Set in the Vercel project settings, never in the repo or in any committed file:
#   DISCORD_CLIENT_ID, DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET, AUTH_SECRET (its own prod value),
#   STDB_LINK_TOKEN (from .env.prod.local after `npm run stdb:bootstrap:prod`), STDB_TARGET=prod
#   (the deployed function refuses any other target), and
# AUTH_ORIGIN=            the site's public origin, scheme and host only, no path and no trailing
#                         slash (for example https://example.com). The only Origin start accepts
#                         and the base of the Discord redirect_uri; not a secret, but required.
# The function holds the link token, never STDB_SERVER_TOKEN.

# Legacy keys from the Next.js app are ignored by everything (nothing reads .env.local).
